{
  "_doc": "Sources read by collect.py. weight 0-20 = how much we trust and value the source. filter=true keeps only items that look like startup/tech-business news (general tech outlets). claim: default claim_status for items from that source. Add a source by appending an entry; kind is one of rss, hn, yc, reddit, youtube, login. youtube: channel_id is the UC... id of the channel (its public feed needs no key); shorts=true keeps Shorts (dropped by default). reddit: subreddits are read together as one public RSS feed of the day's top posts (one request per source, paced by Reddit's rate-limit headers; see RedditFetcher in collect.py). login: optional search on a platform with no public feed (platform xiaohongshu or twitter) through your own logged-in Chrome via agent-reach's OpenCLI bridge; it runs only when agent-reach doctor reports the channel usable (or with collect.py --login-sources) and is otherwise recorded as skipped. keywords are searched one at a time; search_args are passed to `opencli <site> search`. enabled:false skips a source (disabled_reason says why).",
  "_doc_charts": "App Store chart movers (scripts/charts.py), run by collect.py after the sources. countries and charts: Apple's public top-100 feeds read each run; the thresholds are the three lists' rules. Snapshots stay in the local state directory, never in the repo.",
